Description: Order selection for time series models: classical information
    criteria (AIC, AICc, BIC, HQ, FPE, CAT, MDL over Yule-Walker, Burg or
    conditional least-squares fits) side by side with the threshold ("clip")
    estimators of Fine and Hwang (1979) <doi:10.1109/TAC.1979.1102041> built
    on studentized statistics (PACF, Bartlett-studentized ACF, inverse PACF,
    the Jirak (2012) <doi:10.1214/11-AOS963> band, a robust PACF), plus
    McMillan-degree estimators (Bauer's (2001)
    <doi:10.1016/S0005-1098(01)00118-2> SVC on past-future canonical
    correlations, Hankel singular-value thresholding, a sequential rank
    test), ARMA identification (extended sample autocorrelation function,
    Hannan-Rissanen), and the order of integration by sequential unit-root
    testing. All statistics run in a dependency-free Rust core.
